# Plugins

Implementations live in-repo and register by **id**. Selection and order come from **static** inflow (config, CLI, or optional call arguments). Code is not loaded from untrusted paths.

Core `ir/` stays the SSOT (Single Source Of Truth) for named IR kinds (`UIDefinition` today).

## Kinds and execution

| Kind | Execution | Does | Does not |
|---|---|---|---|
| projection | Several stages may be specified, and each specified stage runs | Build a read-only view from restored IR (`componentsByLogicalId`, …) | Mutate IR, persist the view, own vendor serialize |
| writer-filter | Several stages may be specified. After Raw validation, they run in the specified order (`payload → filter → payload`) | Transform validated Raw / residual toward a target payload | Skip Raw validation, talk over an event bus |
| adapter-target | Once per target on that import or export | Reader / Writer / Transformer / schema / target docs for that target | Import into `ir/`, run a second target as another stage |

Several projections and several writer-filters are normal. Adapter-targets are not stages of one pipeline: the selected target runs once.

Projection output is for templates, `arcane:summon`, and optional lookup inside writer-filters.

## Injection

- Registry: `id` → implementation (compile-time)
- Inflow: list of ids, and order where the kind uses order, from `application.yml`, CLI, or optional call arguments. Add a channel only when a caller needs it
- The public API applies the list internally. Callers do not resolve ids and then apply as two required steps. Defaults work with no override; CLI and args override
- Injection selects which registered plugins run. It does not load arbitrary user JS

## Do not

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — named in-repo projections; the API applies the list
const view = applyProjections(snapshot);

// ✅ GOOD — ordered writer-filter stages for one target
const payload = applyWriterFilters(targetId, raw, view);

// ❌ BAD — user JS / out-of-repo module as a plugin
const mod = await import(cliPluginPath);

// ❌ BAD — write projection back into IR / snapshot
snapshot.componentsByLogicalId = view.componentsByLogicalId;

// ❌ BAD — chain another adapter-target as a second stage
await exportTarget(otherTargetId, payload);
```
